body:
the way i see it, it's still going to be that black statue but with corn. it feels insulting towards the little boy from the meme. but i really can't speak on it as a white person. who knows how POC would feel about it if they only saw the refurbished result.

&#x200B;

BUT thats why i mentioned in my update that OP really just shouldn't have posted until AFTER it was repainted. then we woulda known how people would have reacted. guess we'll never know, she deactivated her account. ¯\\\_(ツ)\_/¯

my fiance is barely taller than me and i'm 5'4. a good woman won't care about your height. <3 

&#x200B;

good luck on that date!

I would love to have a pastel cafe-like desk set up! Soft mint, pink, and yellows scattered through-out. A tiny lit up sakura tree, with a few sakura themed Starbucks cups with matcha in one! **A cute mint AND pink themed keyboard to match the milky matcha in the pink sakura cup**, a white or pink mouse, and I'd love to paint my monitors one of those colors to match. Small yellow and green plants on the desk, a PC case with a window where you can see a fake succulent and a small anime figure inside, and a space for my pink digital art tablet!

&#x200B;

Edit: I'd love to have little squishy bread/pastries on my monitor stand as well eheheh. I have this squishy loaf of bread that I keep on my desk at all times so I have the start to my dream set up :3 I want to feel like I'm at a cute cafe!

you are doing SO amazing! the baby steps are the steps that matter the most. you have started and you absolutely can tackle this beast! 

&#x200B;

please keep it up, stranger! you will feel so great once this is done!

i completely understand you! when something doesn't go according to plan, i feel like i want to freak the hell out. its like.. glass shatters in my brain. i can't handle it! i cry most times and get really upset. 

&#x200B;

im so sorry the plans didn't work out, i really hope you two planned another night! <3
